{"name":"Peri Wink","hex":"#b6bdd3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peri","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sprite or supernatural being, often a winged humanoid of immense beauty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peri"},{"term":"wink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To close one's eyes in sleep.","To close one's eyes."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of winking (a blinking of only one eye), or a message sent by winking.","A brief period of sleep; especially forty winks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parī","blocks":[{"text":"A parī or peri is a supernatural entity originating from Persian tales and distributed into wider Asian folklore. The parīs are often described as winged creatures of immense beauty who are structured in societies similar to that of humans. In contrast to jinn, the parīs usually feature in tales involving supernatural elements."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/An_angel%2C_flying%2C_with_cup_and_wine_flask_%28FGA_F1937.7%29.jpg/330px-An_angel%2C_flying%2C_with_cup_and_wine_flask_%28FGA_F1937.7%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Par%C4%AB"},{"title":"Wink","blocks":[{"text":"A wink is a facial expression made by briefly closing one eye. A wink is an informal mode of non-verbal communication usually signaling shared hidden knowledge or intent. However, it is ambiguous by itself and highly dependent upon additional context, without which a wink could become misinterpreted or even nonsensical. For example, in some regions of the world, a wink may be considered rude or offensive. Depending on the relationship of the people involved, a wink could possibly constitute a sexual gesture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gale_Henry.jpg/330px-Gale_Henry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Houris_on_Camelback_-_15th_century_Persia.png/330px-Houris_on_Camelback_-_15th_century_Persia.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Houris_on_Camelback_-_15th_century_Persia.png/330px-Houris_on_Camelback_-_15th_century_Persia.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Houris in paradise, riding camels. From a 15th-century Persian manuscript.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHouris_on_Camelback_-_15th_century_Persia.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Pari_detail_from_Pari_holding_a_unique_animal._19th_cent._Rajput_style_Bhopal_museum_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Pari_detail_from_Pari_holding_a_unique_animal._19th_cent._Rajput_style_Bhopal_museum_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Pari_detail_from_Pari_holding_a_unique_animal._19th_cent._Rajput_style_Bhopal_museum_%28cropped%29.JPG/500px-Pari_detail_from_Pari_holding_a_unique_animal._19th_cent._Rajput_style_Bhopal_museum_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Depiction of a Parī, 19th century, Rajput Bhopal museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APari_detail_from_Pari_holding_a_unique_animal._19th_cent._Rajput_style_Bhopal_museum_(cropped).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Peri_at_the_Gates_of_Paradise%2C_by_Thomas_Crawford%2C_modeled_1854%2C_carved_by_1859_-_Corcoran_Gallery_of_Art_-_DSC01068.JPG/500px-Peri_at_the_Gates_of_Paradise%2C_by_Thomas_Crawford%2C_modeled_1854%2C_carved_by_1859_-_Corcoran_Gallery_of_Art_-_DSC01068.JPG?utm_source=en.w